  "name": "x2-pocket-grab-then-naive",
  "description": "ATTACK: is the dare pocket a wager? A prompt player takes the H capsule and then finishes the slice with the known-winning naive policy. Phase 1 is the p4 policy (hold right + mash Space), which parks the player in the chimney. Phase 2 holds Down across four jump attempts so whichever one lands while standing on the chimney-floor catwalk drops through it onto the y=3 floor - the cheap way past the column-39 step, which a run-jump cannot clear because the chimney-left wall's base sits two tiles above it. Phase 3 runs east off that floor at x=47 into the pocket and collects the reward at x=54. Phase 4 retreats west, hops the +2 step back out, climbs onto the dare overhang's roof and resumes mashing to the rejoin. DESIGN prices this round trip as a wager ('a dead-end round trip plus safety margin fits inside the available crush time'; fixture timing retreatSeconds 1.5 / entryEdgeMarginTiles 18 / minExitMarginTiles 8). What this run reports is what the round trip actually costs in crush margin. Open-loop caveat: the drop-through depends on where phase 1 leaves the player, so this script reproduces the pocket grab in most runs, not all of them - check darePocket.rewardTaken in the report before trusting a single run.",
